{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1042955-random-mundane-encounters-urban-rural","id":1042955,"title":"Random mundane encounters (Urban/Rural)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-03T08:11:21-08:00","id":1042955,"title":"Random mundane encounters (Urban/Rural)","content":"What random encounters do you have to break up a linear Werewolf/Fera story?<br /> <br /> What random encounters do you have or have you used to present an opportunity for humor, sadness , violence etc....? How did they actually play out?<br /> <br /> How can you make humans or a human (regular cookie cutter humans) dangerous for Garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:47:33-08:00","id":1043035,"title":"","content":"I never really use random encounters myself because I have hundreds of ready NPCs created over the last couple dozen years of gaming (though I occasionally have to convert them from another system to cWoD). The waitresses in the restaurant, the drivers in the road, the police on the beat, etc are all characters that can become enemies or allies of the Fera.<br /> <br /> In order to make humans dangerous, I usually make them into Possessed or Sorcerers. The waitresses might belong to a secret coven of witches that maintain mundane identities in order to belay suspicion or belong to a support group of Fomori that seek to avoid descending further into the clutches of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite 'grey' allies/enemies that I use in my games are a group of female fomori sorcerers with high Autonomy that seek to free themselves from the clutches of the Wyrm. They alternate between betraying and helping my players as both groups attack the Wyrm. In fact, some of them have been lovers to the PCs, hiding their corruption with their powers, and secretly feeding information to their group. A few of them are so perfect with their portrayal of normal humans that they have married my PCs and become mothers to Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T12:12:14-08:00","id":1043074,"title":"","content":"I would not make your player's NPC mates betray them. That just makes it difficult to trust anyone in the world played by the GM. Why bother roleplaying a complex relationship with fleshed out characters when it can get upended instantly in favor of a cheap 'gotcha' moment? So many better ways to inflict in-game paranoia on players, without resorting to a 'I control your wife and it turns out she has been working with the enemy the whole tiem lol.'<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1042955-random-mundane-encounters-urban-rural#post1042955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How can you make humans or a human (regular cookie cutter humans) dangerous for Garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a 'damage your health levels' kind of way? You really don't. Humans are dangerous because if you turn them into greasy smears, there is often fallout. People ask questions, cops/Federals get called, and your <i>real</i> enemies might notice.<br /> <br /> Case in point, I had a bunch of buffalo hunters shooting up the prairie, threatening the local Indian tribes who depended on the animals for food, and generally being a deleterious nuisance. My players went and killed them, messily. Body parts all over the place. That is fine and good short term... long term, not so much. When word got back to 'civilization,' the blame for all the carnage and death fell on the 'savages.' The rangers got called in to deal with the native tribes when the Garou were away, and it was a slaughter.<br /> <br /> Garou are great at the close-range, tear 'em to shreds stuff, but they are not quite as good at managing the big picture. Don't constantly outmaneuver your players so that it is frustrating and futile, but make it clear that their burning rage might have far-reaching and unforseen consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T12:40:50-08:00","id":1043096,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Rural:</u></b><br /> <br /> When my Ratkin characters spend too much time in Rodens form in rural areas sitting around bullshitting and arguing about their next move endlessly, I throw an Owl or a Snake at them randomly.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Urban:</u></b><br /> <br /> Gas/Glue/Paint sniffing derelicts aggressively begging<br /> <br /> A dazed prostitute who has wet herself and is looking to score<br /> <br /> Child thieves<br /> <br /> wandering person with a gangrenous leg ( no wyrm funny stuff , just a person without insurance and access to medical care)<br /> <br /> Salty Drunk EMT<br /> <br /> Drive By or Car Crashes<br /> <br /> Rowdy Kids on a schoolbus taunting the driver behind them<br /> <br /> Yuppyscum berating public servants over a ticket etc..<br /> <br /> Know it all hipsters at coffee shops / Bars engaging characters in endless mundane circular arguments<br /> <br /> Skinheads pumping up a youngster to go fuck with regular people as initiation while they watch from behind laughing<br /> <br /> Crusty punks begging and vandalizing property<br /> <br /> The lost foreign tourist<br /> <br /> Overwhelmed single mother asking for help<br /> <br /> Teenagers filming a fight on their phones <br /> <br /> Military men/women on a 3 day weekend ready to raise hell<br /> <br /> someone who drops randomly, convulsing from a stroke / heart attack / Diabetic shock or what have you...<br /> <br /> Pimps/drug dealers/ gangsters/beggars ( no shit , but I feel like someone might say how could you leave this out)<br /> <br /> City Services being lazy, for example Garbage Trucks spilling trash haphazardly<br /> <br /> school field trip","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:22:03-08:00","id":1043113,"title":"","content":"Religious/spiritual person preaching doom<br /> <br /> helicopter news crew<br /> <br /> Exhausted IMPATIENT Detective/ COP/ TAXI DRIVER/ UBER DRIVER/ Emergency Room surgeon<br /> <br /> TACO TRUCK!<br /> <br /> college student protest<br /> <br /> wandering child/toddler in an neighborhood with no parent in sight<br /> <br /> stray dogs /pitbulls<br /> <br /> blind streetside musician<br /> <br /> bug eyed - tight assed pedestrian in a desperate search for a toilet<br /> <br /> people pissing and shitting on the streets<br /> <br /> ski mask /gloves / brass knuckles / knives / rusty screw drivers etc... next to dumpsters or trash cans<br /> <br /> Store / bank robbery<br /> <br /> house burglary<br /> <br /> maids waiting at the bus stop on Friday afternoon<br /> <br /> youngsters rap battling<br /> <br /> ATM mugging<br /> <br /> Crazy/Old/ Vision Impaired &quot;witness&quot; with thick glasses talking to authorities and accusing a character of a crime for no reason<br /> <br /> Bicycle messengers wrestling over a package<br /> <br /> Skateboarders asking you to buy them booze and smokes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12902,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","user":"WISDOMINCHAINS","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:22:42-08:00","id":1043114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1042955-random-mundane-encounters-urban-rural?p=1043096#post1043096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Know it all hipsters at coffee shops / Bars engaging characters in endless mundane circular arguments</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Yikes.</i> Have you no sense of mercy? Your other ideas were fine, but this is way over the top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:31:53-08:00","id":1043119,"title":"","content":"Theres a reason Red Talons and Ratkin are my favorites","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:35:55-08:00","id":1043123,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Urban / Rural</b></u><br /> <br /> Gang of bad attitude Raccoons in a dumpster<br /> <br /> Little bird has fallen from its nest and is slowly twitching to cling to life<br /> <br /> Old wise man feeding pigeons<br /> <br /> <u><b>Urban</b></u><br /> <br /> Diapers thrown in the street<br /> <br /> Bitter doorman with heart of gold<br /> <br /> underpaid secretary just trying to get some fucking lunch<br /> <br /> nervous Intern juggling too many coffee's","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12902,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","user":"WISDOMINCHAINS","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:42:58-08:00","id":1043129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1042955-random-mundane-encounters-urban-rural?p=1043113#post1043113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are really fun lists.<br /> <br /> For Rural/Wilderness stuff:<br /> Random people on Quads/dirt bikes driving/riding through. Accidents/injuries optional.<br /> Campers<br /> Falling Trees<br /> Random lost kids<br /> Hunters/poachers<br /> Pot farmers<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:49:21-08:00","id":1043134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1042955-random-mundane-encounters-urban-rural?p=1043129#post1043129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are really fun lists.<br /> <br /> For Rural/Wilderness stuff:<br /> <br /> Pot farmers<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>haha funny thing (actually not so funny) I just found out recently from a buddy who works in the northwest. Apparently he says up north in cali that random weirdo criminals looking to score will roll on up to these farms and shoot into the air......if they don't hear a shot ringing back up into the air from the farm , then they know its time to raid.<br /> <br /> Now I need to come up with a one shot story for a Child of Gaia Patriarch/Matriarch and his/her kinfolk running one of these farms just so I can throw this encounter at them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T14:13:52-08:00","id":1043146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1042955-random-mundane-encounters-urban-rural?p=1043134#post1043134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> haha funny thing (actually not so funny) I just found out recently from a buddy who works in the northwest. Apparently he says up north in cali that random weirdo criminals looking to score will roll on up to these farms and shoot into the air......if they don't hear a shot ringing back up into the air from the farm , then they know its time to raid.<br /> <br /> Now I need to come up with a one shot story for a Child of Gaia Patriarch/Matriarch and his/her kinfolk running one of these farms just so I can throw this encounter at them</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, most pot farms out here (I'm in the NW now, grew up in NYC) have round the clock armed guards. They're generally just normal people with weapons (no real training), but that's deterrent enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:52:53-08:00","id":1043204,"title":"","content":"Well, the legal growers need guards to keep drug dealers from stealing the stuff. I think it would make a great plot for a group of Children of Gaia Human Kinfolk to be growing medicinal MJ to fund their Garou Kin. They might even have a pack of Wolf Kinfolk on the property to keep down pests that would eat the plants and to chase off trespassers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T16:14:48-08:00","id":1043222,"title":"","content":"In one of my earlier games I had the group wind up stopping a serial killer, and they just realized he was a mundane non supernatural, evil broken human.<br /> <br /> But neighbors and coworkers are always fun go to's for encounters. As well as ghosts of people the group killed. Oh and nosy kids! Toss them in and all of a sudden the pack has to decide how cutthroat they really are in handling mortal bystanders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T17:35:53-08:00","id":1043270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1042955-random-mundane-encounters-urban-rural?p=1043222#post1043222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of my earlier games I had the group wind up stopping a serial killer, and they just realized he was a mundane non supernatural, evil broken human.<br /> <br /> But neighbors and coworkers are always fun go to's for encounters. As well as ghosts of people the group killed. Oh and nosy kids! Toss them in and all of a sudden the pack has to decide how cutthroat they really are in handling mortal bystanders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like giving large doses of mundane in my Garou games.<br /> <br /> In an old Alaskan based game I had a player that made a large metis silverfang with a hunchback. They had a base of operations around a cabin/bar that was run by a kinfolk who was also raising her 3-5 yr old autistic son. One game the metis SF attacked a moose that had wandered into the alley outside the bar, dripping worms, and followed by a cloud of insects.<br /> <br /> The autistic kid looks out his apartment bedroom window (atop the bar) and watches the SilverFang / Moose fomor battle in the alleyway and screams, &quot; MOMMY A POLAR BEAR!&quot;. The kid becomes infatuated with the &quot;polar bear&quot;. From there on out the autistic child ran up to the SF character no matter what form he was in hugging him and calling him Mr. Polar bear.<br /> <br /> Fast forward to the next game and the pack goes out to investigate a hunting lodge nearby (since the moose was tagged). Once they get out there they realize the autistic kid had climbed into the back of their truck to tag along with Mr. Polar bEAR. Fast forward past the attack on the lodge and the pack finds a 3-5 year old metis cub caged in the basement of the hunting lodge. Fast forward to the end of the session and the metis cub attacks/plays to rough with the autistic kid and kill shim............. because the pack was busy arguing about what to do next and who would be responsible for who.........they stopped paying attention to the children.....Garou make bad babysitters.....the cowardly shits never returned to the kinfolks bar too ashamed to face her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:03:32-08:00","id":1043283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1042955-random-mundane-encounters-urban-rural?p=1043270#post1043270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like giving large doses of mundane in my Garou games.<br /> <br /> In an old Alaskan based game I had a player that made a large metis silverfang with a hunchback. They had a base of operations around a cabin/bar that was run by a kinfolk who was also raising her 3-5 yr old autistic son. One game the metis SF attacked a moose that had wandered into the alley outside the bar, dripping worms, and followed by a cloud of insects.<br /> <br /> The autistic kid looks out his apartment bedroom window (atop the bar) and watches the SilverFang / Moose fomor battle in the alleyway and screams, &quot; MOMMY A POLAR BEAR!&quot;. The kid becomes infatuated with the &quot;polar bear&quot;. From there on out the autistic child ran up to the SF character no matter what form he was in hugging him and calling him Mr. Polar bear.<br /> <br /> Fast forward to the next game and the pack goes out to investigate a hunting lodge nearby (since the moose was tagged). Once they get out there they realize the autistic kid had climbed into the back of their truck to tag along with Mr. Polar bEAR. Fast forward past the attack on the lodge and the pack finds a 3-5 year old metis cub caged in the basement of the hunting lodge. Fast forward to the end of the session and the metis cub attacks/plays to rough with the autistic kid and kill shim............. because the pack was busy arguing about what to do next and who would be responsible for who.........they stopped paying attention to the children.....Garou make bad babysitters.....the cowardly shits never returned to the kinfolks bar too ashamed to face her.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually really sad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Poor make believe kid.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T18:17:45-08:00","id":1043288,"title":"","content":"whats worse is that the propriator of the lodge had a daughter who witnessed the garous attack and ran away when they were ripping apart her family. The characters later found out on the local nightly news that she was found unconscious in the woods near frozen to death. The Pack decided to tie up loose ends and went to the hospital through the umbra , fooled/negotiated with the secretary/ reception / front desk spirit of the hospital ( a faceless humanoid with 1950's poofy hair and 8 arms speedily multitasking). The pack went to the girls room in the penumbra and came back to the physical realm. They talked over her body for a minute and decided on a course of action. They smothered her unconscious face with a pillow.<br /> <br /> I remember my jaw was on the floor when they did that. I had not planned for any shit like that. Definitely some world of darkness shit right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T22:11:39-08:00","id":1043861,"title":"","content":"And a rather severe violation of the Litany. They effectively covered up the negligent homicide of a Kinfolk child by murdering an innocent child who would have likely not remembered anything because of the Delirium. Murdering a human witness is not repairing the Veil because murder for expediency brings Garou closer to the Wyrm and makes mortals even more suspicious (the girl who was attacked by a maniac was suffocated to death in the middle of the night, so someone is hiding something), which further threatens the Veil. Discrediting a human witness repairs the Veil because it makes future claims of werewolves even more suspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T04:46:32-08:00","id":1043919,"title":"","content":"Laws get broken all the time. Even more so in the world of darkness. The veil isn't always fool proof also I'd like to add. The garou don't have a reference book to know when something wiped a memory clear or not. <br /> And if your a monster / or a criminal , you wanna tie up loose ends. I was shocked when they did it but it made them monsters and fallible.<br /> <br /> I don't like it when garou are portrayed as knights in shining armor. I like blurred morality . I like when monsters are still monsters despite what cultural rules get slapped on them to toe the line. To me it's just like life on the street but more brutal and leaves you feeling dirtier even when your trying to do the right thig shit happens...and if it can be helped , most people will sweep something under the rug or go to lengths to protect their reputation. More so I believe when renown is on the line and your a monster that's part of a modern day savage society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12902,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","user":"WISDOMINCHAINS","date":". 02-05-2017, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:59:29-08:00","id":1044575,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Rural</b></u><br /> <br /> Hermit in the woods<br /> <br /> escaped con / fugitive<br /> <br /> Bonfire partying highschool drunks trying to score after the &quot;big game/graduation&quot;<br /> <br /> Stepping on an old rusty forgotten hunters trap<br /> <br /> Walking past those infared hunters cameras<br /> <br /> Wild hogs feasting at a feeder<br /> <br /> Unused hunters blinds/stands<br /> <br /> Quiet suicide by hanging<br /> <br /> Starving and weak animals<br /> <br /> Rabid squirrels<br /> <br /> Stumbling on to a military base in the midst of Field Training Excercises","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}